paragraph.content:
all Members shall
                dress
                in business attire and behave with decorum;

Members shall not read newspapers, books, letters or other documents, except
                such matter therein as may be directly connected with the business of the
                Council;

the President or Chairman shall first call upon those Members who are in
                    favour of the question to raise their hands, and shall then call upon those who
                    are against the question to raise their hands;

the President or Chairman shall first call upon Members who are in favour
                    of the question to raise their hands, and shall then call upon those who are
                    against the question to raise their hands;

subject to paragraph (e), notice of resumption of debate shall be given by
                    the Member or public officer in charge of the bill not less than 12 clear days
                    before the day on which the debate is to be resumed;

the President or the chairman of a committee or any other presiding Member (as
                the case may be) shall have all the powers as provided for in the current provisions
                of the Rules of Procedure;
